IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgh-formation`

-- Tests for sgh-formation.l4 (ss 17 and 18). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the run.

§ `s 17: formation of companies`
-- (test alias a17a = `s 17(1) the person may form an incorporated company`)
-- arguments: subscribed the person's name or names to a constitution; complied with the requirements as to registration
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the person may form an incorporated company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "by subscribing the person's name or their names to a constitution and complying with the requirements as to registration, form an incorporated company"
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the person may form an incorporated company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not subscribed: the text says nothing of forming one another way
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the person may form an incorporated company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- requirements as to registration not complied with: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a17b = `s 17(2) a company may be of this kind`)
#ASSERT `s 17(2) a company may be of this kind` `limited by shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) a company limited by shares"
#ASSERT `s 17(2) a company may be of this kind` `limited by guarantee` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) a company limited by guarantee"
#ASSERT `s 17(2) a company may be of this kind` `unlimited` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) an unlimited company"
#ASSERT `s 17(2) a company may be of this kind` `limited by shares and by guarantee` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list does not say "only" (list not closed)
-- (test alias a17c = `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred`)
-- arguments: the number of persons the body consists of; formed to carry on a business with gain as its object; the body is a company; registered as a company under this Act; formed pursuant to another written law or letters patent; an association or partnership formed for a profession or calling that written law restricts to the qualified
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 21 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "No company, association or partnership consisting of more than 20 persons may be formed for the purpose of carrying on any business that has for its object the acquisition of gain": 21 persons
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- exactly 20 persons: the bar is on "more than 20"; the text says nothing of 20 or fewer
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 21 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no business for gain: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 21 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless it is registered as a company under this Act"
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 21 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "or is formed pursuant to some other written law in Singapore or letters patent"
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 21 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (4): an association or partnership formed for a qualified profession or calling: "does not apply"
#ASSERT `s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` 21 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (4) speaks of "an association or a partnership", not a company: the bar stands for a company
-- (test alias a17d = `s 17(5) the company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act`)
-- arguments: the company is limited by guarantee with a share capital; the date of registration
#ASSERT `s 17(5) the company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act` TRUE (Date 15 8 1984) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "As from 15 August 1984": the day itself is inside
#ASSERT `s 17(5) the company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act` TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after that date
#ASSERT `s 17(5) the company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act` TRUE (Date 14 8 1984) EQUALS NOTHING   -- before that date: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 17(5) the company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act` FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING   -- another kind of company: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a17e = `s 17(6) the prohibition in subsection (5) affects the company`)
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the prohibition in subsection (5) affects the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is registered as such before 15 August 1984"
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the prohibition in subsection (5) affects the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other company: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a17f = `s 17(6) section 38(2) continues to apply to the company`)
#ASSERT `s 17(6) section 38(2) continues to apply to the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "section 38(2) continues to apply to a company so registered"
#ASSERT `s 17(6) section 38(2) continues to apply to the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other company: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a17g = `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires`)
-- arguments: such a company; the date the company elects; the election is to a company limited by shares or by guarantee
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` TRUE (Date 15 8 1984) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 2 years of that date": the day itself is in time (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` TRUE (Date 15 8 1986) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day: 15 August 1984 plus 2 years
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` TRUE (Date 16 8 1986) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day later: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` TRUE (Date 14 8 1984) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before "that date": outside the period
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` TRUE (Date 15 8 1985) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an election to be a company limited by shares or by guarantee
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` FALSE (Date 15 8 1985) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such a company: the duty is on "any such company"
-- (test alias a17h = `s 17(6) the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired`)
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` (Date 15 8 1986) EQUALS FALSE   -- the last day of the 2 years is not yet past
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` (Date 16 8 1986) EQUALS TRUE   -- the day after the last day
#ASSERT `s 17(6) the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` (Date 1 1 1980) EQUALS FALSE   -- before the period began
-- (test alias a17i = `s 17(7) the conversion of the company is effected`)
-- arguments: a company referred to in subsection (6); special resolution lodged with the Registrar; constitution altered to conform
#ASSERT `s 17(7) the conversion of the company is effected` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "effected by lodging with the Registrar a special resolution ... and altering its constitution"
#ASSERT `s 17(7) the conversion of the company is effected` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no special resolution lodged: the text does not say "only"
#ASSERT `s 17(7) the conversion of the company is effected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- constitution not altered: the text does not say "only"
#ASSERT `s 17(7) the conversion of the company is effected` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a company referred to in subsection (6): the text says nothing
-- (test alias a17j = `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes`)
-- arguments: complied with subsection (7); the Registrar issued a notice of incorporation in accordance with the special resolution; the kind of company the special resolution determines
#ASSERT `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` TRUE TRUE `limited by shares` EQUALS JUST `limited by shares`   -- "the company becomes a company limited by shares"
#ASSERT `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` TRUE TRUE `limited by guarantee` EQUALS JUST `limited by guarantee`   -- "or a company limited by guarantee, as the case may be"
#ASSERT `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` TRUE TRUE `limited by shares and by guarantee` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the text names no other result
#ASSERT `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` TRUE TRUE `unlimited` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the text names no other result
#ASSERT `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` TRUE FALSE `limited by shares` EQUALS NOTHING   -- no notice of incorporation issued: a failed "On" returns no value
#ASSERT `s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` FALSE TRUE `limited by shares` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not complied with subsection (7): a failed "On" returns no value
-- (test alias a17k = `s 17(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation`)
-- arguments: the company has applied; the prescribed fee has been paid
#ASSERT `s 17(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee"
#ASSERT `s 17(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- fee unpaid: a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT `s 17(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application: a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet

§ `s 18: private company`
-- (test alias a18a = `s 18(1)(b) the number of members counted against the limit`)
-- arguments: persons who hold shares, each joint holding counted once; of those, in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary; of those, former employees who have continued to be members
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) the number of members counted against the limit` 60 5 3 EQUALS 52   -- "not counting any person in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary or any person who while previously in the employment ... was and thereafter has continued to be a member": 60 less 5 less 3
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) the number of members counted against the limit` 50 0 0 EQUALS 50   -- no one to leave out
-- (test alias a18b = `s 18(1) the company may be incorporated as a private company`)
-- arguments: the company has a share capital; the constitution restricts the right to transfer its shares; the number of members to which the constitution limits the company
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company may be incorporated as a private company` TRUE TRUE 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "limits to not more than 50 the number of its members": exactly 50
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company may be incorporated as a private company` TRUE TRUE 51 EQUALS NOTHING   -- 51 is more than 50: a failed "if" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company may be incorporated as a private company` TRUE FALSE 50 EQUALS NOTHING   -- no restriction on the transfer of shares: a failed "if" gating a grant
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company may be incorporated as a private company` FALSE TRUE 50 EQUALS NOTHING   -- "A company having a share capital": the text says nothing of one with none
-- (test alias a18c = `s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18`)
-- arguments: has a share capital; the constitution restricts the right to transfer its shares; the number of members to which the constitution limits the company; the notice of incorporation states that it is a private company
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` TRUE TRUE 50 TRUE EQUALS TRUE   -- all conditions met
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` TRUE TRUE 51 TRUE EQUALS FALSE   -- the constitution allows 51 members
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` TRUE FALSE 50 TRUE EQUALS FALSE   -- no restriction on the transfer of shares
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` FALSE TRUE 50 TRUE EQUALS FALSE   -- no share capital
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` TRUE TRUE 50 FALSE EQUALS FALSE   -- the notice of incorporation does not state that it is a private company
-- (test alias a18d = `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision`)
-- arguments: on 29 December 1967 a private company by virtue of paragraph (a) of the definition in s 4(1); the constitution does not contain the restrictions and limitations required by (1); the provision; the constitution already contains the provision
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` TRUE TRUE `s 18(2) a restriction on the right to transfer its shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the constitution of the company is deemed to include each such restriction or limitation that is not so included"
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` TRUE TRUE `s 18(2) a limitation on the number of its members` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the limitation on the number of members
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` TRUE TRUE `s 18(2) a restriction on the right to transfer its shares` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- already included: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` TRUE TRUE `s 18(2) any other provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "required by subsection (1)": the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` FALSE TRUE `s 18(2) a restriction on the right to transfer its shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a private company by virtue of paragraph (a) on that day: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` TRUE FALSE `s 18(2) a restriction on the right to transfer its shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the constitution already contains what (1) requires: a failed "Where"
-- (test alias a18e = `s 18(2) the deemed restriction prohibits the transfer of shares`)
-- arguments: a restriction deemed to be included under (2); the transfer is to a person approved by the directors
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the deemed restriction prohibits the transfer of shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "a restriction that prohibits the transfer of shares except to a person approved by the directors of the company"
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the deemed restriction prohibits the transfer of shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except to a person approved by the directors": the exception
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the deemed restriction prohibits the transfer of shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other restriction: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a18f = `s 18(3) the deemed restriction or limitation prevails over the provision to the extent of the inconsistency`)
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the deemed restriction or limitation prevails over the provision to the extent of the inconsistency` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "that restriction or limitation, to the extent of the inconsistency, prevails"
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the deemed restriction or limitation prevails over the provision to the extent of the inconsistency` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no inconsistency: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the deemed restriction or limitation prevails over the provision to the extent of the inconsistency` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a restriction or limitation deemed to be included under (2): a failed "Where"
-- (test alias a18g = `s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration`)
-- arguments: a private company; by special resolution; an alteration of a restriction on transfer or a limitation on the number of members; after it the constitution ceases to include the limitation required by (1)(b)
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "A private company may, by special resolution, alter any restriction ... or any limitation"
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "but not so that the constitution of the company ceases to include the limitation required by subsection (1)(b)"
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a private company: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by special resolution: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an alteration of another provision: the text says nothing

§ `Regulative rules of ss 17 and 18`
-- s 17(6): "within 2 years of that date": 730 days from 15 August 1984.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 17(6) rule: the company's duty to elect to convert and re-register` (Company "Old Guarantee Ltd") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Old Guarantee Ltd" DOES `s 17(6) elect to convert and re-register the company either as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee` AT 730
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 17(6) rule: the company's duty to elect to convert and re-register` (Company "Old Guarantee Ltd") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Old Guarantee Ltd" DOES `s 17(6) elect to convert and re-register the company either as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee` AT 731
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 17(6) rule: the company's duty to elect to convert and re-register` (Company "Old Guarantee Ltd") AT 0 WITH
    (`WAITUNTIL` 731)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 17(6) rule: the company's duty to elect to convert and re-register` (Company "Old Guarantee Ltd") AT 0 WITH
-- s 17(9): no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no breach path.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 17(9) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue the certificate of confirmation of incorporation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 17(9) issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 17(9) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue the certificate of confirmation of incorporation` AT 0 WITH
